## 2. Scene System (Roblox Studio-Style)

### 2.1 Instance Hierarchy

The scene graph is a tree of instance objects, similar to Roblox's Instance class.

Core instance fields:
- name: string
- class_name: string
- parent: instance*
- children: vector<instance*>
- archivable: bool
- locked: bool
- visible: bool

Core instance methods:
- set_parent(instance* new_parent)
- find_first_child(const string& child_name)
- find_first_child_of_class(const string& class_name)
- find_first_ancestor(const string& ancestor_name)
- get_children()
- get_descendants()
- destroy()
- clone()
- register_properties(property_registry& registry)
- on_property_changed(const string& property_name)

Events:
- child_added
- child_removed
- descendant_added
- descendant_removed
- ancestry_changed
- destroyed

### 2.2 Workspace

workspace is the root of the scene tree, equivalent to Roblox's Workspace.

Fields:
- gravity: vector3
- distributed_game_time: float

Methods:
- set_gravity(const vector3& g)
- get_gravity()
- raycast(const ray& r, float max_distance)

### 2.3 Part (3D Object)

Transform fields:
- position: vector3
- size: vector3
- rotation: vector3 (Euler angles in degrees)
- orientation: quaternion
- pivot_offset: vector3

Appearance fields:
- color: vector3
- transparency: float
- reflectance: float
- surface_material: material_enum
- texture: texture_handle*

Physics fields:
- anchored: bool
- can_collide: bool
- can_query: bool
- can_touch: bool
- mass: float
- velocity: vector3
- angular_velocity: vector3

Shape fields:
- shape: part_shape_enum (block, sphere, cylinder, wedge, corner_wedge, mesh)
- custom_mesh: mesh*

Events:
- touched
- touch_ended
- clicked

Default: can_collide = true, anchored = false, can_query = true, can_touch = true.
Any 3D object can be a physics object. Physics is enabled by default. Disable via anchored = true (kinematic) or can_collide = false (no collision).

