## 10. Build System

### 10.1 Build Scripts

setup.bat (Windows) and setup.sh (Linux/macOS):

Downloads and sets up all dependencies into ./libs/:

1. Clone/pull vcpkg repository
2. Install packages via vcpkg: glfw3, glad, joltphysics, stb, luau (or build from source), miniaudio (single header, download)
3. Clone raylib (or use vcpkg if available)
4. Download/build Luau from https://github.com/luau-lang/luau
5. Set up environment variables
6. Generate compile_flags.txt for clangd

build.bat (Windows) and build.sh (Linux/macOS):

Builds the engine and editor:
1. Detect platform
2. Set compiler to Clang
3. Use vcpkg toolchain
4. Compile all src/engine/ and src/editor/ files
5. Link against all libs
6. Output: bin/forestium3d_editor.exe (or .app on macOS)

build_game.bat (Windows) and build_game.sh (Linux/macOS):

Packages a game project:
1. Read project settings from .f3dproj file
2. Compile game runtime (src/game_runtime/)
3. Copy engine binaries (without editor code)
4. Process assets: import, optimize, pack into .pak files
5. XOR encrypt .pak files with project key
6. Optional: compress with 7zip before XOR
7. Generate executable with embedded icon
8. Output structure:
```
my_game/
├── my_game.exe
├── forestium3d.dll / libforestium3d.so
├── luau_vm.dll
├── fmod.dll (if using FMOD)
├── assets/
│   ├── core.pak
│   ├── levels.pak
│   ├── audio.pak
│   └── textures.pak
└── config.ini
```

### 10.2 Compiler and Build Tool

- Compiler: Clang (LLVM)
- Package Manager: vcpkg (NOT CMake as build system -- use raw Clang compilation or a simple build script)
- Build files: compile_flags.txt for clangd, simple batch/shell scripts for building
- No CMake -- the user explicitly requested NOT to use CMake

